  "body": "Property Documents can be downloaded here: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/KHYG\r\n\r\nRoom for the cars, space for the toys, and a home that's been beautifully cared for.\r\nRight in the heart of Whangaparaoa, tucked away in a quiet street with an elevated outlook, this loved home delivers a combination that's hard to beat. With a double internal-access garage and generous off-street parking for around four additional vehicles, there's room for the cars, the boat, the campervan and everything in between!\r\nThe owners have taken meticulous care of the property's exterior, which presents well and reflects the attention it has received over the years. The combination of monolithic and Paliside weatherboard cladding, complemented by features such as eaves and external guttering, contributes to the home's overall appearance. It is evident the property has been well maintained, with pride of ownership clearly reflected in its presentation.\r\nStep inside and discover a well-maintained three-bedroom home offering a practical, family-friendly layout and plenty of potential to add your own touches over time. The separate lounge provides a comfortable space to relax, while the open-plan kitchen and dining area captures the morning sun, creating a warm and welcoming hub for everyday living. North-facing and filled with natural light, the home enjoys an elevated outlook across the surrounding area, with scope to modernise and personalise to suit your own style.\r\nThe master bedroom features its own ensuite and good storage, while two further bedrooms, a family bathroom, separate toilet and generous hallway storage complete the accommodation. Whether you're a first-home buyer, a couple wanting extra space, or a family juggling teenagers, vehicles and busy lifestyles, there's plenty here to appreciate.\r\nOutside, the easy-care gardens keep maintenance to a minimum, while the covered pergola is perfect for summer barbecues, family gatherings and Christmas celebrations. There's even more to discover beneath the home, where a dry, substantial storage and workshop area offers excellent space for tools, hobbies and all those extras that need a home of their own. A section of the workshop floor has also been concreted, adding further practicality to this versatile space.\r\nCentrally located, the elevated setting captures all-day sunshine, a prized northerly aspect, and a tranquil atmosphere. Just moments away are the golden sands of Arkles Bay and Stanmore Bay, Coast Plaza, supermarkets, Mitre 10, popular cafés, respected schools and excellent transport links incl Penlink, placing every daily amenity and coastal attraction within easy reach. \r\nLooking for your first home? Ready to add to your investment portfolio or keen to downsize and enjoy an easier lifestyle? Whatever your next move looks like, could this be the one you've been waiting for?",
